    Refine dispatch model: waste-to-energy, verified inputs, calibration fixes (#1)
    
    Harden the 2025/2030 Kraftwerksstrategie PyPSA dispatch model and regenerate
    all results and figures from the finalized configuration.
    
    Model & config (config.py, model.py):
    - Add waste-to-energy as a real must-run carrier (~1.3 GW), removing the coal
      back-fill artefact; calibrates to within 0.2% of realised 2025 output.
    - Correct 2025 CO2 price to the realised ~75 EUR/t (was 67), improving the
      mean-price calibration from -4.4% to +1.1%.
    - Use authentic net-public Energy-Charts benchmarks and the real ARA API2
      hard-coal price (no forced numbers); document the residual coal gap.
    - Raise VOLL to 4000 EUR/MWh; enable negative prices via EEG bidding.
    - Add a missing-money calculation and an islanded adequacy bracket; replace the
      empty scarcity figure (fig5) with a 4-case A/B x imports/islanded chart.
    - Remove all [VERIFY] tags after checking inputs against primary sources.
    
    Results & docs:
    - Regenerate results/*.csv and figures/*.png; add fig8/fig9 calibration plots.
    - Refresh README from the current results; add CLAUDE.md project guidance.
    
    Headline 2030 A->B effect: mean price -9%, volatility -10%, CO2 -15%,
    imports -90%, islanded unserved energy -93%, total system cost -2.5%.
    report.docx is a local deliverable, gitignored per repo convention.
    
    Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

